# Line-ending policy.
#
# The remote service script is deployed to a LINUX host and executed by bash. A
# CRLF there produces "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M" or mysterious `$'\r'`
# errors, so shell scripts must stay LF in the repository and in the working
# tree regardless of the committer's platform.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
